 "e9a_summary": "# E9a: latency, throughput, compute and bandwidth (FRED test, k=1 unless stated)\n\n| Method | median time to first detection | p90 | detected within 0.25 s | real-time factor (proc / data time, k=1) | compute |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Event: PropPulse + learned classifier | 120 ms | 1308 ms | 62% of 238 | 0.45x | CPU signal processing (not FLOP-counted) |\n| Event: YOLO on event frames | 33 ms | 1333 ms | 67% of 238 | 3.10x | YOLO11n 6.5 GFLOPs x tiles (6 at 1280x720) x 30 Hz |\n| Frame: U-Net CNN | 267 ms | 2713 ms | 34% of 238 | 3.82x | 123 GFLOPs x 30 fps |\n| Frame: RGB YOLO | 33 ms | 1553 ms | 50% of 238 | 3.99x | YOLO11n 6.5 GFLOPs x 6 tiles x 30 fps |\n| Frame: classical | 267 ms | 1293 ms | 5% of 238 | 7.48x | ~0.05 GFLOPs x 30 fps |\n\n**Notes:** time to first detection is measured from the first annotated frame of each drone track in a 4 s clip, at the method's 5%-FA threshold. Real-time factor < 1 means faster than real time. Hardware: Apple M3 (events: Python, 1 CPU core; CNN/YOLO: MPS GPU).\n\n## Data rates\n\n| Stream | Rate |\n|---|---|\n| Events (FRED test, median per clip) | 89 k ev/s = 0.7 MB/s @ 8 B/event (EVT3 encoding ~2-4 B/event: 0.3 MB/s) |\n| Events, p90 clip | 1497 k ev/s = 12.0 MB/s |\n| RGB 1280x720 @30 fps raw | 82.9 MB/s (grey 27.6 MB/s) |\n| RGB H.264 (typical surveillance bitrate) | ~0.5-1 MB/s, but compression hurts tiny targets (stress test: CNN FA 0.11 -> 0.53 with JPEG) |",
 "e9b_summary": "# E9b: spiking propeller resonator vs FFT verifier (real FRED test windows, k=1)\n\nWindows: 71053 (5398 on drones, 65655 off-drone) from 50 clips. RF bank: 48 neurons, 120-1000 Hz, Q=30, spike at 3.0 sigma.\n\n| Verifier | ROC AUC (drone vs not) | decision time | ops per window (median) | energy per window (estimate) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| FFT harmonic comb (current) | 0.688 | end of window: median 210 ms | 4.59e+05 (FLOP-like) | 2.11 uJ |\n| Spiking RF bank (event-driven) | 0.682 | first spike on drones: median 37 ms | 1.89e+04 (synaptic updates) | 0.02 uJ |\n\n- RF spikes also occur off-drone: 40% of off-drone windows spike (median first spike 92 ms) vs 83% of drone windows. A first spike is evidence, not a decision; decision latency at matched FA needs the confirmation rule.\n- Combined (FFT score + RF score, rank-averaged) AUC: 0.761\n- RF bank CPU time (numba, this Mac): median 0.79 ms per window.\n- Energy column = operation count x 45 nm per-op energy (0.9 pJ accumulate, 4.6 pJ MAC; Horowitz 2014). It is an **estimate for neuromorphic/ASIC-style execution, not a measurement**. On a CPU both cost far more.\n- An RF-neuron update is a complex multiply-accumulate per event per neuron, so its op cost is understated by counting it as one accumulate; a conservative bound is ~4 MACs per update.",
